<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tripoli</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tripoli is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> and historically a major northern terminus of trans-Saharan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a>. Goods from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-sudan">central Sudan</a>, including slaves, leather and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, passed through it to Mediterranean markets. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> note that Sokoto's commercial network was connected to Tripoli and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> via the desert routes.</p></div>
